                <pb facs="0324" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.24/1099: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-17T09:00:00+02:00">December 17, 1941—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 18—3:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1972. Your 757, December 10, 5 p.m. Am I authorized to inform the Egyptian
                    authorities that lend-lease has been extended to Egypt and if so, is there any
                    pertinent information which I should convey at that time?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
